# Design System & Concepts

The Tuff design system is not a mere collection of visual tokens, but a rigorous engineering contract built upon **perceptual ergonomics**, **modern streaming computation**, and **high-velocity productivity discipline**.

This section systematically breaks down the "why" and "how" behind every design decision across the unified TDS token system, geometry, material physics, color science, typography, micro-motion, and AI streaming interactions.

## Tuff Design System (TDS)

- **[Tuff Design System (TDS) & Live Token Inspector](/en/concepts/tds)** — Single-source `tokens.json`, `#141414` dark neutral base, default `refraction` surface, live WCAG 2.1 0.85 contrast checker, 3-layer Theme Packs, and the Core 36 primitives matrix.

## Geometry and Curvature

- **[G2 Continuous Curvature & Squircle Geometry](/en/concepts/curvature)** — Moving beyond standard `border-radius` fillets, explaining curvature jumps, superellipse formulas, and Apple smooth corners.
- **[Concentric Radii & Inset Clearance](/en/concepts/concentricity)** — The $R_{\text{outer}} = R_{\text{inner}} + \text{Padding}$ conservation law, caret clipping prevention, and 0.65x vertical optical padding.
- **[Open-Order Z-Index & Sticky Dividers](/en/concepts/depth-topology)** — Eliminating `z-index: 99999` chaos: overlays take numbers from one counter in the order they open, drawers first lift it to 10000, and the 1px line divider rule.

